{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     home/path-card — NSDS's .ns-path__card: one COURSE, as a destination.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     TAKES THE COURSE'S OVERVIEW POST, not its tag.

     The obvious version queries tags and renders one card each. It cannot
     work: a tag query has no way to say "tags that have a #course post under
     them", so courses and training sections come back in the same list and
     the two bands render identically. Querying `filter="tag:hash-course"`
     returns exactly the course overview posts, each carrying its own title,
     url, excerpt and primary tag — the right data, and the right URL without
     deriving it.

     It also avoids a {{#get}} PER CARD for the lesson count. That count lives
     on the course page, where the children are already in scope; here it
     would be one query per card and — as the course hero proved — a second
     {{#get}} in a nested position tends to return nothing at all.

     The glyph is inferred from the primary tag's slug; see
     internal/topic-icon for why that inference lives in one place.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
<a class="ns-path__card" href="{{url}}">
    <span class="ns-tthumb ns-tthumb--glyph">{{#primary_tag}}{{> "internal/topic-icon"}}{{/primary_tag}}</span>
    <span class="ns-path__title">{{title}}</span>
    {{#if excerpt}}<span class="ns-path__text">{{excerpt}}</span>{{/if}}
    <span class="ns-path__meta">
        <span class="sp-optional">{{~> "internal/level"~}}</span>
        <span class="sp-duration sp-optional">{{~> "internal/duration"~}}</span>
    </span>
</a>
